---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Showcase from "../../../components/Showcase.astro";
import type { UsageTree } from "@skryensya/core/usage-tree";

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/vanilla @skryensya/react`;

/*
 * The demo, as a USAGE TREE. The markup below the stage, the TSX beside it and the live React
 * island are all emitted from this, so the snippet a reader copies is what they just saw render.
 */
const tree = {
  contract: "segmented",
  signature: "Segmented",
  options: { value: "day" },
  attrs: { "aria-label": "Range" },
  slots: {
    items: [
      { options: { value: "day" }, slots: { label: "Day" } },
      { options: { value: "week" }, slots: { label: "Week" } },
      { options: { value: "month" }, slots: { label: "Month" } },
    ],
  },
} as const satisfies UsageTree;

const js = `import { initComponents } from "@skryensya/vanilla/auto";

await initComponents();`;
---

<Base title="SegmentedControl" description="SegmentedControl: unique and visible choice over a small group, with radiogroup semantics.">
  <h1>SegmentedControl</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    SegmentedControl is a single choice of a small, fixed set, shown at once: a radiogroup with button bar clothing. To navigate between panels use <a href="/en/components/tabs">Tabs</a>; for many options or free text, <a href="/en/components/select">Select</a>.
  </p>

  <Showcase tree={tree} label="Segmented" />
  <p>
    The vanilla enhancer selects with click and arrows; <code>Home</code> and <code>End</code> jump to the first and last segment. The chosen option is <code>data-value</code> and is announced with <code>aria-checked</code>. Each segment paints <code>--size-control-sm</code> and retains a hit from <code>44px</code> via <code>:: after</code> (the indicator follows the painted box).
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />

  <h2>Initialize vanilla</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={js} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>The code is in the <strong>React</strong> tab of the preview. It is controlled (<code>value</code>) or uncontrolled (<code>defaultValue</code>); When changing, the indicator aligns and travels to the new option with the state change motion token.</p>
</Base>
